/src/bad.rs:2: `sokf-implements: req-none` refers to the id `req-none`, which no document carries (SOKF_FORMAT_145)
/src/bad.rs:3: `sokf-implements: req-cli#nothing` refers to a fragment that is neither a captured key nor a heading (SOKF_FORMAT_145)
/src/bad.rs:4: `sokf-implements:` has no reference after it, or has a word after its reference. A marker holds exactly one reference (SOKF_FORMAT_144)
/src/bad.rs:5: `sokf-implements:` has no reference after it, or has a word after its reference. A marker holds exactly one reference (SOKF_FORMAT_144)
/src/bad.rs:10: `sokf:ignore-end` appears outside an ignore region (SOKF_FORMAT_153)
/src/bad.rs:11: `sokf-implements: nostore:req-cli` refers to the store `nostore`, which is not a knowledge store in this repository (SOKF_FORMAT_145)
/src/bad.rs:12: `sokf-foo_bar:` has a rel that isn't kebab case. Write the rel as lowercase words of letters and digits joined by `-`, such as `sokf-implements:` (SOKF_FORMAT_143)
